{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuU6J9EvW5QsRLq4CTrF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've built the dashboard and created the alert rule, and both exist in Kibana. The rule is enabled and has already run once with status `ok`.\n\n**1. What the data holds**\n\nThe `kibana_sample_data_logs` data view has one document per HTTP request, with `timestamp` as its time field. The main fields are:\n- **Request:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `referer`, `agent`\n- **Outcome:** `response`, the status code stored as a string, and `bytes`, the response size\n- **Client:** `clientip`, `geo.src` / `geo.dest` (country codes), `geo.coordinates` and `machine.os`\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags`, `memory`, `machine.ram`, `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-86e79169 Web logs overview\"**\n\nIt has seven panels: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-86e79169-web-logs-overview-633370b3dd70\n- Total requests (single number)\n- Unique visitors (distinct client IPs)\n- Requests over time, split by response code (bar chart)\n- Share of requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Bytes transferred over time (line chart)\n- Top 10 requested URLs, with request count and average bytes (table)\n- Top 10 source countries (bar chart)\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-86e79169 5xx spike\"** (id `dbf22dd2-8409-4a40-9a7a-cb57b61687d4`)\n- **Type:** Elasticsearch query, on the `kibana_sample_data_logs` index and the `timestamp` field.\n- **Query:** matches any `response.keyword` value starting with \"5\", so it catches every 5xx code.\n- **Condition:** fires when there are more than 10 matching requests in the last 5 minutes, checked every minute.\n- **Notifications:** none are attached, so when it fires it only shows up as an alert inside Kibana. You'll need to add an action, such as Slack or email, if you want to be notified.\n\nI couldn't count the response codes directly (Kibana blocked the query I tried), so I haven't checked that 5xx codes actually appear in this data. The sample data normally contains 503s, which the rule's query would match."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":21903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"286f8275-3550-4b38-acf7-5b80da11d321","timestamp":"2026-10-11T00:01:43.408Z","request_id":"req_011CfuU6HxKpktwDBdqhv4d9"}
